<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayabhata IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 730s</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayabhata IV was the last known king of the Gurjara dynasty of Nandipuri, which ruled the Lata region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>. Known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-plate grants, he fought the Arab raids from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> in the 730s. The dynasty disappears from the record around 738, probably overwhelmed by these incursions and by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalukya-dynasty">Chalukyas</a>, and Lata later passed to the Rashtrakutas.</p></div>
